{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat control-reader-brief.md controls/control-packet-3.json'","aggregated_output":"# Stage B: reading the control theses (read-only)\n\nYou are an independent reader. Do not edit files, run model calls or start runs, and do not read any file other than this brief\nand the one packet you are given.\n\nEach item of your packet pairs a **ruler question** (a question written by hand for an earlier, frozen measurement, with its\nunit, due day and ladder of rungs) with a **judged question** the system wrote itself for a thesis it opened (its question, the\noutcome it looks at, due day, year and rungs). It also lists **reader B's decisive items**: the evidence an earlier reader, called\nreader B, cited for the frozen answer to the ruler question (each with its day, title, passage and meaning), and **the evidence\nshown to the judge**: every evidence entry the system's judge was shown for the judged question in any of its requests on or\nbefore 2026-07-14 (empty when there is none). You are not told either answer, and you do not judge which answer is right.\n\nFor each item, answer three questions.\n\n1. `same_question`: **yes** when the judged question asks what the ruler question asks: the same quantity measured the same way\n   (the same total, scope and unit: not a part of it, a ceiling on it, another quantity or another unit), or the same event,\n   for the same period. **no** otherwise. Wording may differ; a judged question that asks for more or less than the ruler's,\n   or for another period, is **no**.\n2. `same_due`: for an **event** (a yes-or-no question), **yes** only when the judged question's deadline is the ruler's\n   deadline. For a **figure**, **yes** when the two due days both mark the publication of the same period's figure (for\n   example, both the annual report of the same fiscal year, even if the two days differ); **no** otherwise.\n3. `items`: for **each** of reader B's decisive items, by its id, **shown** when its content is present in the evidence shown to\n   the judge (the same fact or figure, in any wording, from any source), **not_shown** when it is absent. Search the entries for\n   the figure or the fact; do not mark an item shown because a related item is.\n\nReturn one JSON object per item, one per line, in packet order, and nothing else (no prose, no code fence):\n`{\"control\": 3, \"same_question\": \"yes\"|\"no\", \"same_due\": \"yes\"|\"no\", \"items\": {\"i005\": \"shown\"|\"not_shown\", ...}, \"why\": \"one sentence naming what decides each no and each not_shown\"}`.\n\n## Third reader (only where the two readers differ)\n\nA third reader of each family is given this brief, the packet, and a list of the disputed points, each a control number and a\nfield (`same_question`, `same_due`, or `item <id>`), without the two readers' answers. For each point, answer that one question\nafresh by the rules above and return one JSON object per point, one per line, and nothing else:\n`{\"control\": 3, \"field\": \"item i005\", \"ruling\": \"yes\"|\"no\"|\"shown\"|\"not_shown\", \"why\": \"one sentence\"}` (`yes`/`no` for the two\nquestion fields, `shown`/`not_shown` for an item).\n[\n {\n  \"control\": 6,\n  \"ruler_question\": {\n   \"question\": \"What will Nvidia's total revenue be in FY2027?\",\n   \"unit\": \"USD\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $500 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 500000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": null\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $400 billion and below $500 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 400000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 500000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $350 billion and below $400 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 350000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 400000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $300 billion and below $350 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 300000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 350000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is below $300 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": 300000000000.0\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"judged_question\": {\n   \"view_id\": \"v11\",\n   \"question\": \"What will NVIDIA report as total revenue for FY2027?\",\n   \"looks_at\": \"NVIDIA FY2027 total revenue\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\",\n   \"year\": \"FY2027\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\"\n  },\n  \"judged_rungs\": [\n   {\n    \"position\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n    \"condition\": \"Total revenue is at least $450 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": 450000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": null\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n    \"condition\": \"Total revenue is at least $400 billion but less than $450 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": 400000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 450000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 3,\n    \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n    \"condition\": \"Total revenue is at least $350 billion but less than $400 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": 350000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 400000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 4,\n    \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n    \"condition\": \"Total revenue is at least $300 billion but less than $350 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": 300000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 350000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 5,\n    \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n    \"condition\": \"Total revenue is less than $300 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": null,\n    \"hi\": 300000000000.0\n   }\n  ],\n  \"reader_b_decisive_items\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i281\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-09\",\n    \"title\": \"DeepSeek Just Dealt Nvidia Stock a Potentially Major Blow\",\n    \"passage\": \"forecasting revenue of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%, and a non-GAAP gross margin of about 75%\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"NVIDIA\",\n     \"what\": \"Q2 FY2027 revenue and gross-margin guidance\",\n     \"how_much\": \"$91 billion ±2%; non-GAAP gross margin about 75%\",\n     \"period\": \"Q2 FY2027\",\n     \"condition\": \"assumes no China Data Center compute revenue\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i295\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-10\",\n    \"title\": \"Here are Friday's biggest analyst calls: Nvidia, SpaceX, Toll, Shopify, Twilio, Seagate, Chipotle & more\",\n    \"passage\": \"the company describing \\\"accelerating growth rates\\\" even as revenues approach the $100 bn per quarter mark\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"NVIDIA management, relayed by Morgan Stanley\",\n     \"what\": \"revenue growth rates accelerating\",\n     \"how_much\": \"quarterly revenue approaching $100 bn\",\n     \"status\": \"claim\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i106\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-05\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia's next-gen AI rack system delayed to 2028 on manufacturing snags, SemiAnalysis says\",\n    \"passage\": \"SemiAnalysis also projects Nvidia's data-center compute revenue will run 20% above Wall Street consensus in the second half of fiscal 2027\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"SemiAnalysis\",\n     \"what\": \"NVIDIA data-center compute revenue versus Wall Street consensus\",\n     \"how_much\": \"20% above consensus\",\n     \"period\": \"second half of fiscal 2027\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i219\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Vera Rubin rack costs $7.8M — memory is why\",\n    \"passage\": \"First shipments are scheduled for the third quarter of 2026, with volume ramping in the fourth.\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"what\": \"Vera Rubin VR200 NVL72 first shipments and volume ramp\",\n     \"period\": \"first shipments Q3 2026; volume ramp Q4 2026\",\n     \"status\": \"plan\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i037\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-02\",\n    \"title\": \"Microsoft vs. Nvidia: Which Is the Better AI Stock to Own for the Next 3 Years?\",\n    \"passage\": \"from trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion to $392 billion this fiscal year, and $554 billion the following year\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"Wall Street analysts\",\n     \"what\": \"NVIDIA total revenue estimates\",\n     \"how_much\": \"$392 billion this fiscal year, $554 billion next year (from $253 billion trailing twelve months)\",\n     \"period\": \"this fiscal year (FY2027) and the following year (FY2028)\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   }\n  ],\n  \"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\": [\n   \"- e112 [third_party_view; finance.yahoo.com; original source Unnamed analysts ; from gnews:b40db2c507df72ec016e99e6 2026-07-08] Unnamed analysts expect NVIDIA total revenue to reach $392.7 billion in FY2027.\\n    Quote: analysts are anticipating further gains of $392.7 billion in its current fiscal year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e120; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e119 [third_party_view; TradingView; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:a09988fd9c5c1a739a14f873 2026-07-08] Bloomberg Intelligence data cited by TradingView put Nvidia's server GPU market share at 97% at the end of 2025, up from 95% at the end of 2024.\\n    Quote: Nvidia's market position still appears strong, with the company holding 97% of the server GPU market at the end of 2025, up from 95% at the end of 2024, according to Bloomberg Intelligence data cited in the source.\",\n   \"- e120 [third_party_view; TradingView; original source TradingView 2026-07-08; from gnews:a09988fd9c5c1a739a14f873 2026-07-08] The report said Nvidia was projected to generate $393 billion in sales in FY2027, up 82%, and $228 billion in profit, up 90%; the profit estimate had risen 13% over the preceding three months.\\n    Quote: The company is projected to generate $228 billion in profit on $393 billion in sales in fiscal 2027, which ends Jan. 31, representing expected growth of 90% and 82%, respectively, while its profit estimate has risen 13% over the past three months.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e112; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e124 [fact; TechCrunch author Russell Brandom, describing data via Ornn; original source Ornn ; from gnews:3ea4e94c707ece2db2d7caec 2026-07-09] Ornn's spot-market data showed the price of an hour of Nvidia H100 compute peaking at around $3.20 in May 2026 and then steadily declining.\\n    Quote: Just like Nvidia’s stock price, there’s a peak in May (around $3.20 an hour) and then a steady drop-off.\",\n   \"- e125 [third_party_view; Ornn co-founder and CTO Wayne Nelms, quoted by TechCrunch author Russell Brandom; original source Wayne Nelms, Ornn co-founder and CTO ; from gnews:3ea4e94c707ece2db2d7caec 2026-07-09] Ornn co-founder and CTO Wayne Nelms said current memory-market conditions would likely persist absent a major HBM breakthrough, a supply-demand shift, or a new memory-market entrant.\\n    Quote: “Until there’s a major technological breakthrough on HBM [high-bandwidth memory], a shift in supply and demand, or someone new [enters the market in memory], I think things will more or less persist as we see today.”\",\n   \"- e129 [fact; Adam Spatacco; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:931ee0196ca609e637235fad 2026-07-09] Nvidia reported record data-center segment revenue in the first quarter; the amount is not stated.\\n    Quote: Revenues from Nvidia's data center segment -- the primary engine of the business -- set a record in the first quarter.\",\n   \"- e130 [party_statement; Adam Spatacco; original source Nvidia management ; from gnews:931ee0196ca609e637235fad 2026-07-09] Nvidia management guided to faster revenue growth in the second quarter; the measure and amount are not specified.\\n    Quote: Moreover, management guided for further revenue growth acceleration for the second quarter.\",\n   \"- e131 [party_statement; Adam Spatacco; original source Nvidia management ; from gnews:931ee0196ca609e637235fad 2026-07-09] Nvidia management cited roughly $1 trillion of revenue visibility for Blackwell and Vera Rubin processors across 2026 and 2027, anchored by multiyear customer commitments.\\n    Quote: Management has also articulated roughly $1 trillion in revenue visibility for its Blackwell and Vera Rubin processors across 2026 and 2027, anchored by multiyear commitments from hyperscalers and large enterprise customers.\",\n   \"- e132 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Rick Munarriz 2026-07-09; from gnews:b412380d12c5a222545d42f1 2026-07-09] The author says NVIDIA’s revenue growth accelerated for three consecutive quarters; no revenue amounts are given.\\n    Quote: Nvidia's revenue has accelerated for three consecutive quarters.\",\n   \"- e133 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b412380d12c5a222545d42f1 2026-07-09] NVIDIA’s fiscal first-quarter revenue increased 85% year over year, its strongest growth rate in a year and a half.\\n    Quote: The 85% top-line jump it posted in its fiscal first quarter is the strongest increase in a year and a half.\",\n   \"- e134 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Rick Munarriz 2026-07-09; from gnews:b412380d12c5a222545d42f1 2026-07-09] The author expects NVIDIA’s growth to decelerate and its margins may contract as rivals improve their hardware alternatives.\\n    Quote: Nvidia's growth will decelerate at this point, and margins may contract as rivals improve their hardware alternatives.\",\n   \"- e138 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Bloomberg Intelligence projected NVIDIA would hold 70% to 75% of the AI chip market through 2030.\\n    Quote: Bloomberg Intelligence projects the company will hold 70% to 75% of the AI chip market through 2030.\",\n   \"- e139 [party_statement; qz.com; original source Andy Jassy, Amazon CEO ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Amazon CEO Andy Jassy said in late 2025 that Trainium2 had no spare capacity and was a multibillion-dollar business growing at a 150% quarterly clip.\\n    Quote: Amazon CEO Andy Jassy said in late 2025 that Trainium2, the previous generation, had no spare capacity left to sell. He said it had grown into a multibillion-dollar business at a 150% quarterly clip.\",\n   \"- e140 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source qz.com 2026-07-09; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] The article said Amazon's Trainium4 chip could arrive later in 2026.\\n    Quote: Amazon 's next chip, Trainium4, which packs three times the performance of its predecessor, could arrive later this year.\",\n   \"- e141 [party_statement; qz.com; original source Microsoft ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Microsoft said Maia 200 will power OpenAI's newest models and Microsoft's AI products, including Copilot.\\n    Quote: The chip will power OpenAI's newest models, along with Microsoft 's own AI products, such as Copilot.\",\n   \"- e142 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source qz.com 2026-07-09; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Meta planned to build three more MTIA chip generations over the next two years for running generative AI models.\\n    Quote: Meta is set to build three more generations over the next two years with the purpose of running generative AI models.\",\n   \"- e143 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source qz.com 2026-07-09; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Meta's MTIA 450 was expected to arrive in early 2027.\\n    Quote: The next one, MTIA 450, arrives in early 2027, doubling how fast the chip moves data in and out of memory.\",\n   \"- e144 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source qz.com 2026-07-09; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Meta's MTIA 500 was expected to arrive later in 2027.\\n    Quote: Its eventual successor, MTIA 500, is expected to come later next year, and pushes memory speed another 50% higher.\",\n   \"- e145 [fact; qz.com; original source OpenAI and Broadcom ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] OpenAI and Broadcom announced in October 2025 a plan to build 10 gigawatts of custom AI chips.\\n    Quote: It announced a partnership with Broadcom in October 2025 to build 10 gigawatts of custom AI chips, a measure of how much power the new chips will draw once installed.\",\n   \"- e146 [fact; qz.com; original source Tesla ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Tesla completed the AI5 inference chip design in April 2026 and planned production at TSMC's Arizona plant and Samsung's Texas plant.\\n    Quote: Tesla finished the design of its AI5 inference chip in April 2026, according to Reuters . Production is planned at both TSMC 's plant in Arizona and Samsung's plant in Texas.\",\n   \"- e147 [party_statement; qz.com; original source Tesla ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Tesla targeted mid-2027 for AI5 mass production.\\n    Quote: Tesla is targeting mid-2027 for mass production.\",\n   \"- e148 [fact; qz.com; original source SpaceX ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] SpaceX filed plans in May for a $55 billion Texas chip plant called Terafab, with total investment potentially reaching $119 billion.\\n    Quote: SpaceX, Musk's other property, filed plans in May for a $55 billion chip manufacturing plant in Texas called Terafab, Reuters reported . Total investment in the plant could reach $119 billion.\",\n   \"- e149 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source SpaceX ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] The planned Terafab plant would use a manufacturing process licensed from Intel.\\n    Quote: The plant would use a manufacturing process licensed from Intel $INTC .\",\n   \"- e150 [fact; qz.com; original source Broadcom ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Broadcom reported $5.2 billion in AI-related revenue for fiscal 2025's third quarter.\\n    Quote: The company reported $5.2 billion in AI-related revenue for the third quarter of its 2025 fiscal year.\",\n   \"- e151 [third_party_view; Gizmodo, relaying Tom’s Hardware; original source Tom’s Hardware ; from gnews:fe9210b7b43c51e0939ecbbb 2026-07-09] Tom’s Hardware reported that large data-center projects including OpenAI’s Stargate are calling for hundreds of thousands of additional DRAM wafers per month, roughly 40% of global DRAM output.\\n    Quote: huge data center projects like OpenAI’s Stargate are calling for hundreds of thousands more DRAM wafers per month, amounting to roughly 40% of global DRAM output.\",\n   \"- e152 [fact; Gizmodo; original source Micron ; from gnews:fe9210b7b43c51e0939ecbbb 2026-07-09] Micron decided to wind down its Crucial consumer brand to focus on data-center demand.\\n    Quote: Micron even decided to wind down its consumer business brand , Crucial, to focus on data center demand.\",\n   \"- e155 [party_statement; au.finance.yahoo.com; original source Cerebras ; from gnews:66cb0387229ac4b1390615cb 2026-07-09] Cerebras plans to bring its first European data-centre capacity online by end-2026 and build a European network with 200 MW of combined power capacity by end-2027, expanding AI-compute competition in NVIDIA’s market.\\n    Quote: US-based artificial intelligence chip maker Cerebras said on Thursday that it plans to bring its first European data centre capacity online by the end of 2026, followed by a rapid expansion across France and the Nordics, boosting its AI computing capacity in Europe.\",\n   \"- e156 [third_party_view; Andrew Feldman, quoted by au.finance.yahoo.com; original source Andrew Feldman, Cerebras CEO ; from gnews:66cb0387229ac4b1390615cb 2026-07-09] Cerebras CEO Andrew Feldman said its European data-centre expansions would be worth several billion dollars.\\n    Quote: “These are massive expansions” worth several billion dollars, chief executive Andrew Feldman told AFP on the sidelines of the RAISE Summit in Paris.\",\n   \"- e157 [party_statement; au.finance.yahoo.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:66cb0387229ac4b1390615cb 2026-07-09] NVIDIA said its technology powers more than 90% of announced AI factory projects in Europe.\\n    Quote: The expansion comes as AI infrastructure investment accelerates across Europe, where Nvidia says its technology powers more than 90% of the continent's announced AI factory projects.\",\n   \"- e119 [third_party_view; TradingView; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:a09988fd9c5c1a739a14f873 2026-07-08] Bloomberg Intelligence data cited by TradingView put Nvidia's server GPU market share at 97% at the end of 2025, up from 95% at the end of 2024.\\n    Quote: Nvidia's market position still appears strong, with the company holding 97% of the server GPU market at the end of 2025, up from 95% at the end of 2024, according to Bloomberg Intelligence data cited in the source.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e158; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e120 [third_party_view; TradingView; original source TradingView 2026-07-08; from gnews:a09988fd9c5c1a739a14f873 2026-07-08] The report said Nvidia was projected to generate $393 billion in sales in FY2027, up 82%, and $228 billion in profit, up 90%; the profit estimate had risen 13% over the preceding three months.\\n    Quote: The company is projected to generate $228 billion in profit on $393 billion in sales in fiscal 2027, which ends Jan. 31, representing expected growth of 90% and 82%, respectively, while its profit estimate has risen 13% over the past three months.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e112, e159; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e133 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b412380d12c5a222545d42f1 2026-07-09] NVIDIA’s fiscal first-quarter revenue increased 85% year over year, its strongest growth rate in a year and a half.\\n    Quote: The 85% top-line jump it posted in its fiscal first quarter is the strongest increase in a year and a half.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e161, e170, e172; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e158 [third_party_view; Jeran Wittenstein, citing Bloomberg Intelligence data; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:49f225cd79fb22132f3b9ee4 2026-07-10] Bloomberg Intelligence data put Nvidia’s server GPU market share at 97% at year-end 2025, up from 95% at year-end 2024.\\n    Quote: Nvidia had 97% of the server GPU market at the end of 2025, up from 95% at the end of 2024, according to data compiled by Bloomberg Intelligence.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e119; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e159 [third_party_view; Jeran Wittenstein, citing Bloomberg data; original source Bloomberg ; from gnews:49f225cd79fb22132f3b9ee4 2026-07-10] Bloomberg data project NVIDIA FY2027 profits of $228 billion, up 90%, and sales of $393 billion, up 82%.\\n    Quote: chipmaker is projected to deliver $228 billion in profits on sales of $393 billion in fiscal 2027, which ends Jan. 31. That would represent an expansion of 90% and 82%, respectively, according to data compiled by Bloomberg.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e120; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e160 [third_party_view; Trefis; original source Wall Street consensus ; from gnews:6abaf2856736877236d30f6a 2026-07-10] Wall Street consensus expects NVIDIA revenue to grow about 32% annually over the next few years.\\n    Quote: Wall Street consensus sees NVIDIA’s revenue growing about 32% a year for the next few years.\",\n   \"- e161 [fact; Trefis; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:6abaf2856736877236d30f6a 2026-07-10] NVIDIA revenue grew 71% over the last twelve months and 85% in the most recent quarter.\\n    Quote: revenue grew 71% over the last twelve months and 85% in the most recent quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e133; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e162 [party_statement; Trefis; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:6abaf2856736877236d30f6a 2026-07-10] NVIDIA guided revenue for the upcoming quarter to a midpoint of $91.00 billion.\\n    Quote: For the upcoming quarter, the company guided revenue to a midpoint of $91.00 billion, signaling continued strong demand.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e168; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e163 [party_statement; Trefis; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:6abaf2856736877236d30f6a 2026-07-10] NVIDIA management said the Vera CPU opens a new total addressable market of $200 billion for NVIDIA.\\n    Quote: Management sees its new Vera CPU opening a “brand new $200 billion TAM for NVIDIA,” a market it has never addressed before.\",\n   \"- e164 [third_party_view; Trefis; original source Trefis 2026-07-10; from gnews:6abaf2856736877236d30f6a 2026-07-10] Trefis calculated that at a share price of about $202.78, NVIDIA trades at 13.3 times analysts’ expected FY2029 earnings, 41% below the current-year earnings multiple.\\n    Quote: At today’s share price of about $202.78, the multiple you are paying on those future earnings falls to just 13.3 times. That is a 41% lower multiple than this year’s, a phenomenon known as the forward valuation discount.\",\n   \"- e165 [third_party_view; Trefis; original source Trefis 2026-07-10; from gnews:6abaf2856736877236d30f6a 2026-07-10] Trefis’s scenario analysis estimated NVIDIA shares would be about 35% higher if the stock traded at 17.9 times FY2029 earnings.\\n    Quote: For example, if the multiple settles at about 17.9 times 2029’s earnings, midway between today’s 22.6 and that 13.3 floor, the stock would trade about 35% higher than it does today.\",\n   \"- e166 [fact; gurufocus.com, relaying Reuters; original source Meta ; from gnews:09b9d76297a57f198651c5e7 2026-07-10] Reuters reported that Meta plans to begin manufacturing its Iris custom AI processor in September 2026; it is designed with Broadcom and will be made by TSMC, and Meta intends it to complement rather than replace its Nvidia and AMD GPUs.\\n    Quote: Reuters said Meta plans to begin manufacturing its custom AI processor, code-named Iris, in September after completing initial testing. The chip is being designed with Broadcom (AVGO) and manufactured by Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing (TSM). The report said the processor is intended to support Meta's AI infrastructure while complementing, rather than replacing, the large number of graphics pro\",\n   \"- e167 [fact; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Data Center revenue of $75.246 billion, up 92% year over year, and networking revenue growth of 199% in Q1 FY2027.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue hit $75.246 billion, up 92% year over year, and networking alone grew 199%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e173, e193; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e168 [party_statement; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] NVIDIA guided to revenue of $91 billion for Q2 FY2027.\\n    Quote: Q2 FY27 guidance points to $91 billion in revenue.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e162; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e170 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja) 2026-07-10; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] The author cited NVIDIA revenue growth of 85.23% year over year and a non-GAAP gross margin of 75.0%.\\n    Quote: For a business growing revenue 85.23% year over year at 75.0% non-GAAP gross margins, that is cheap on any historical comparison.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e133, e174, e192; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e171 [rumour; GuruFocus; original source GuruFocus 2026-07-10; from gnews:4c201dc59ba0c7579bfef4db 2026-07-10] The article reported concerns that major NVIDIA clients, including Meta, were shifting toward developing their own AI chips; the claim was presented as a concern, not a confirmed plan.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA's stock surge comes amidst growing concerns that major clients, such as Meta, are shifting towards developing their own AI chips.\",\n   \"- e172 [fact; 247WallSt. (David Moadel); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially, including Data Center revenue of $75.2 billion.\\n    Quote: The company reported record revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially, with Data Center revenue reaching $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e133; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e173 [fact; 247WallSt. (David Moadel); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA Data Center Networking revenue was $14.8 billion in Q1 FY2027, up 199% year over year.\\n    Quote: Within that segment, Data Center Networking alone hit $14.8 billion, up 199% from a year earlier, reflecting surging demand for the Spectrum-X Ethernet and NVLink interconnect systems that travel with every rack-scale Blackwell deployment.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e167; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e174 [party_statement; 247WallSt. (David Moadel); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 non-GAAP gross margin of 75% and guided Q2 FY2027 revenue to $91 billion.\\n    Quote: Non-GAAP gross margin came in at 75%, and management guided Q2 FY2027 revenue to $91 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e170; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e175 [party_statement; 247WallSt. (David Moadel); original source NVIDIA management (outlook assumption); 247WallSt. (upside interpretation) ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA's Q2 FY2027 revenue outlook assumed zero Data Center compute revenue from China; the article says a thaw in H200 export policy could add upside.\\n    Quote: Notably, that outlook assumed zero Data Center compute revenue from China, meaning any policy thaw on H200 exports could represent additional upside.\",\n   \"- e177 [fact; 247WallSt. (David Moadel); original source NVIDIA (revenue figure); 247WallSt. (growth assessment) ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported FY2026 revenue of $215.9 billion; the author says sustaining comparable percentage growth becomes harder from that base.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA’s FY2026 revenue reached $215.9 billion, and sustaining comparable percentage growth becomes mathematically harder from that starting point.\",\n   \"- e179 [fact; The Verge; original source Counterpoint ; from gnews:3839887e5ca53a0cb0e7c91e 2026-07-10] Counterpoint data put SK Hynix’s share of the global DRAM market at 29%, Samsung’s at 38%, and Micron’s at 22% as of June 2026.\\n    Quote: As of June 2026, SK Hynix makes up 29 percent of the global DRAM market, with Samsung at 38 percent and Micron at 22 percent, according to data from Counterpoint .\",\n   \"- e180 [party_statement; The Verge, reporting Bloomberg’s account of Chey Tae-won’s statement; original source SK Group chairman Chey Tae-won ; from gnews:3839887e5ca53a0cb0e7c91e 2026-07-10] SK Group chairman Chey Tae-won said SK Hynix plans to increase memory-chip capacity over the next five years to address a shortage that could last until 2030.\\n    Quote: SK Group chairman Chey Tae-won said in June that the company plans to ramp up its memory chip capacity over the next five years to address a shortage that could last until 2030, Bloomberg reports .\",\n   \"- e181 [third_party_view; Kristina Partsinevelos, as quoted by 24/7 Wall St.; original source Counterpoint Research ; from gnews:9ae96ca750b8e3962c47795f 2026-07-10] Kristina Partsinevelos, citing Counterpoint Research, said SK Hynix held roughly 58% of the high-bandwidth-memory market, with Micron and Samsung at roughly 21% each.\\n    Quote: SK Hynix is the world leader in high bandwidth memory . The memory that feeds AI chips with roughly 58% of that market. Micron and Samsung competitors split roughly 21% each … as per Counterpoint Research.\",\n   \"- e182 [third_party_view; Kristina Partsinevelos, as quoted by 24/7 Wall St.; original source Kristina Partsinevelos 2026-07-10; from gnews:9ae96ca750b8e3962c47795f 2026-07-10] Kristina Partsinevelos said SK Hynix revenue was expected to triple to $235 billion in 2026 and that the company was committing more than $720 billion in capital investment over the coming years, primarily in South Korea.\\n    Quote: Partsinevelos noted revenue is expected to triple to $235 billion this year, with the company committing over $720 billion in capital investment over the coming years, primarily in South Korea.\",\n   \"- e183 [third_party_view; Kristina Partsinevelos, as quoted by 24/7 Wall St.; original source Kristina Partsinevelos 2026-07-10; from gnews:9ae96ca750b8e3962c47795f 2026-07-10] Kristina Partsinevelos forecast that new SK Hynix high-bandwidth-memory supply would not arrive before late 2027, prolonging the shortage and keeping prices at record highs for now.\\n    Quote: “None of that supply, though, arrives before late 2027, which keeps the memory shortage going and record-high prices intact for now,” Partsinevelos said.\",\n   \"- e184 [fact; 24/7 Wall St.; original source Micron Technology ; from gnews:9ae96ca750b8e3962c47795f 2026-07-10] Micron reported Q3 FY2026 revenue of $41.456 billion, up 345.7% year over year, non-GAAP diluted EPS of $25.11, and GAAP gross margin of 84.6%.\\n    Quote: Micron posted Q3 FY2026 revenue of $41.456 billion, up 345.7% year over year, with non-GAAP diluted EPS of $25.11 and GAAP gross margin of 84.6%.\",\n   \"- e185 [party_statement; 24/7 Wall St.; original source Micron Technology ; from gnews:9ae96ca750b8e3962c47795f 2026-07-10] Micron guided to following-quarter revenue of $49.0 billion to $51.0 billion.\\n    Quote: Guidance for the following quarter calls for revenue of $50.0 billion plus or minus $1.0 billion.\",\n   \"- e186 [fact; 24/7 Wall St.; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:9ae96ca750b8e3962c47795f 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.62 billion, up 85.2% year over year, Data Center revenue of $75.25 billion, and total supply-related commitments of $119.0 billion.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.62 billion, up 85.2% year over year, with Data Center revenue of $75.25 billion and total supply-related commitments of $119.0 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e169; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e187 [rumour; wccftech.com; original source wccftech.com, relaying an unnamed report ; from gnews:170f44b2067e0405a5f5528a 2026-07-10] An unnamed report says NVIDIA has put prepared RTX 50 SUPER cards on hold while it evaluates 3 GB GDDR7 memory pricing; at least one board partner reportedly received cards.\\n    Quote: However, the latest report claims that the products are already prepared and that at least one board partner has received RTX 50 SUPER cards, but NVIDIA has placed them on hold while it evaluates the pricing of 3 GB GDDR7 memory.\",\n   \"- e188 [rumour; wccftech.com; original source wccftech.com, relaying an unnamed report ; from gnews:170f44b2067e0405a5f5528a 2026-07-10] wccftech.com reports that the 3 GB GDDR7 modules expected for the RTX 5070 Ti SUPER reportedly cost $60–$70 each, versus around $20 for current 2 GB modules.\\n    Quote: Realistically, the RTX 5070 Ti SUPER could command a larger premium over the RTX 5070 Ti than initially expected, especially since the 3 GB GDDR7 modules required for its 24 GB configuration reportedly cost between $60 and $70 each, compared to around $20 for current 2 GB modules.\",\n   \"- e189 [party_statement; tikr.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] Nvidia estimates that about 20% of its business comes from supporting frontier AI models, including those built by OpenAI and Anthropic.\\n    Quote: To put some numbers behind that, Nvidia estimates about 20% of its business comes from supporting frontier AI models built by companies like OpenAI and Anthropic.\",\n   \"- e190 [third_party_view; tikr.com; original source TD Cowen ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] TD Cowen estimates that enterprise applications across multiple industries account for a low-to-mid-teens share of Nvidia’s revenue.\\n    Quote: Meanwhile, TD Cowen estimates that Nvidia’s revenue from enterprise applications across multiple industries is in the low-to-mid-teens range.\",\n   \"- e191 [third_party_view; tikr.com; original source TD Cowen ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] TD Cowen cited climbing rental prices for older GPU models as evidence of tight computing capacity.\\n    Quote: Rental prices for older GPU models have been climbing\",\n   \"- e192 [fact; tikr.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] Nvidia reported $82 billion in total revenue, up 85% year over year, for the quarter; it was the third consecutive quarter of accelerating growth.\\n    Quote: The company posted $82 billion in total revenue, up 85% year-over-year, marking its third straight quarter of accelerating growth.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e170; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e193 [fact; tikr.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] Nvidia reported $75 billion in data-center revenue for the quarter, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data center revenue alone hit $75 billion, up 92% year over year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e167; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e194 [party_statement; tikr.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] Nvidia expects its Vera CPU line to generate $20 billion in sales by the end of this fiscal year.\\n    Quote: the company expects to generate $20 billion in sales by the end of this fiscal year\",\n   \"- e195 [fact; tikr.com; original source Perplexity ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] Perplexity chose to use Nvidia’s new CPUs for AI-agent tasks.\\n    Quote: AI startup Perplexity has also chosen to use Nvidia’s new CPUs for AI agent tasks.\",\n   \"- e196 [third_party_view; tikr.com; original source Mark Zuckerberg ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] Meta CEO Mark Zuckerberg commented that progress in AI agents was slower than expected.\\n    Quote: Comments from Meta’s Mark Zuckerberg about slower-than-expected progress in AI agents have also added caution to the broader AI narrative.\",\n   \"- e197 [third_party_view; tikr.com; original source Bank of America ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] Bank of America views the recent semiconductor-sector pullback as a temporary adjustment rather than evidence that AI demand is fading.\\n    Quote: Still, firms like Bank of America view the recent semiconductor sector pullback as a temporary adjustment rather than a sign that AI demand is fading\",\n   \"- e198 [third_party_view; es.tradingview.com; original source Morgan Stanley ; from gnews:1bfc0e875ab1f26dcf48fb06 2026-07-11] Morgan Stanley said AI laboratories account for roughly 20% of NVIDIA’s demand, with enterprise AI adoption expanding beyond hyperscale cloud providers.\\n    Quote: The bank noted that AI laboratories now account for roughly 20% of Nvidia’s demand, highlighting how enterprise AI adoption is expanding beyond hyperscale cloud providers.\",\n   \"- e158 [third_party_view; Jeran Wittenstein, citing Bloomberg Intelligence data; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:49f225cd79fb22132f3b9ee4 2026-07-10] Bloomberg Intelligence data put Nvidia’s server GPU market share at 97% at year-end 2025, up from 95% at year-end 2024.\\n    Quote: Nvidia had 97% of the server GPU market at the end of 2025, up from 95% at the end of 2024, according to data compiled by Bloomberg Intelligence.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e119, e218; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e161 [fact; Trefis; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:6abaf2856736877236d30f6a 2026-07-10] NVIDIA revenue grew 71% over the last twelve months and 85% in the most recent quarter.\\n    Quote: revenue grew 71% over the last twelve months and 85% in the most recent quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e133, e205; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e168 [party_statement; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] NVIDIA guided to revenue of $91 billion for Q2 FY2027.\\n    Quote: Q2 FY27 guidance points to $91 billion in revenue.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e162, e221, e239; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e172 [fact; 247WallSt. (David Moadel); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially, including Data Center revenue of $75.2 billion.\\n    Quote: The company reported record revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially, with Data Center revenue reaching $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e133, e219; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e181 [third_party_view; Kristina Partsinevelos, as quoted by 24/7 Wall St.; original source Counterpoint Research ; from gnews:9ae96ca750b8e3962c47795f 2026-07-10] Kristina Partsinevelos, citing Counterpoint Research, said SK Hynix held roughly 58% of the high-bandwidth-memory market, with Micron and Samsung at roughly 21% each.\\n    Quote: SK Hynix is the world leader in high bandwidth memory . The memory that feeds AI chips with roughly 58% of that market. Micron and Samsung competitors split roughly 21% each … as per Counterpoint Research.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e226; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e193 [fact; tikr.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] Nvidia reported $75 billion in data-center revenue for the quarter, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data center revenue alone hit $75 billion, up 92% year over year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e167, e220; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e201 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source Silicon Analysts ; from gnews:2beadbce40c7f927f33d9fc5 2026-07-12] Silicon Analysts estimated that Nvidia held more than 90% of the AI training-chip market in 2025.\\n    Quote: According to Silicon Analysts , which compiles estimates from TrendForce, Morgan Stanley $MS , and TSMC $TSM capacity data, Nvidia 's share exceeded 90% in training in 2025.\",\n   \"- e202 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source Silicon Analysts ; from gnews:2beadbce40c7f927f33d9fc5 2026-07-12] Silicon Analysts estimated Nvidia's AI inference-chip market share at 60% to 75% in 2025.\\n    Quote: Its inference share sat between 60% and 75% over the same period, undercut by growing competition from custom silicon.\",\n   \"- e203 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source TechCrunch ; from gnews:2beadbce40c7f927f33d9fc5 2026-07-12] TechCrunch reported that 1.4 million Amazon Trainium chips across three generations were deployed as of March, including more than one million Trainium2 chips running Anthropic's Claude.\\n    Quote: As of March, 1.4 million Trainium chips were deployed across three generations, according to TechCrunch , with Anthropic's Claude running on more than one million Trainium2 chips alone.\",\n   \"- e204 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source Mizuho Securities and Silicon Analysts ; from gnews:2beadbce40c7f927f33d9fc5 2026-07-12] Mizuho Securities estimated Nvidia's overall AI-chip market share at 70% to 95% depending on segment; Silicon Analysts projected it would settle near 75% as the total market grows beyond $200 billion.\\n    Quote: Nvidia 's overall AI chip market share, estimated by Mizuho Securities at between 70% and 95% depending on segment, is projected by Silicon Analysts to settle near 75% as the total market expands past $200 billion.\",\n   \"- e205 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:07cf5835d106467db5448c13 2026-07-12] Nvidia reported revenue growth of 85% in its past quarter.\\n    Quote: During its past quarter, Nvidia's revenue increased at an 85% clip.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e161; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e206 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:07cf5835d106467db5448c13 2026-07-12] Wall Street analysts expect Nvidia revenue to grow 96% in Q2.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts expect 96% growth during Q2.\",\n   \"- e208 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-12; from gnews:07cf5835d106467db5448c13 2026-07-12] The author believes Nvidia likely already has orders on the books for 2027, giving it visibility into demand.\\n    Quote: I'm more inclined to believe Nvidia over the market's skepticism, as it likely has orders on the books for next year, so it can easily see the demand already.\",\n   \"- e209 [rumour; tech-insider.org; original source The Information ; from gnews:8faf69f198e10f14aae67621 2026-07-12] Nvidia reportedly shelved the RTX 50 Super refresh, including the completed-design 24GB RTX 5080 Super, in December 2025.\\n    Quote: According to The Information, Nvidia quietly shelved its planned RTX 50 “Super” refresh back in December 2025 — including a 24GB RTX 5080 Super that had reportedly reached completed-design stage\",\n   \"- e210 [rumour; tech-insider.org; original source The Information ; from gnews:8faf69f198e10f14aae67621 2026-07-12] Nvidia’s next-generation RTX 60-series gaming GPUs have reportedly slipped to a 2028 launch from an earlier rumored late-2027 launch.\\n    Quote: reporting from The Information corroborated by Tom’s Hardware and Yahoo Finance.\",\n   \"- e211 [rumour; tech-insider.org; original source Unnamed supply-chain sources, as reported by tech-insider.org ; from gnews:8faf69f198e10f14aae67621 2026-07-12] Nvidia reportedly plans to cut RTX 50-series card production by 15% to 20% through at least Q3 2026.\\n    Quote: Nvidia is reportedly cutting production of existing RTX 50-series cards already on shelves by an estimated 15% to 20% through at least Q3 2026\",\n   \"- e212 [rumour; tech-insider.org; original source Unnamed sources, as reported by tech-insider.org ; from gnews:8faf69f198e10f14aae67621 2026-07-12] Nvidia’s RTX 5060 has reportedly been pulled from retail for at least six months.\\n    Quote: The entry-level RTX 5060 has taken the hardest hit, reportedly pulled from retail entirely for at least six months .\",\n   \"- e213 [third_party_view; tech-insider.org; original source CNBC ; from gnews:8faf69f198e10f14aae67621 2026-07-12] Samsung, SK Hynix, and Micron reportedly sold out their entire 2026 HBM output under long-term contracts.\\n    Quote: all three manufacturers have reportedly sold out their entire 2026 HBM output under long-term contracts, according to CNBC’s reporting from January 2026.\",\n   \"- e214 [third_party_view; tech-insider.org; original source Unnamed forecasters, as reported by tech-insider.org ; from gnews:8faf69f198e10f14aae67621 2026-07-12] HBM demand is projected to grow roughly 70% year over year in calendar 2026.\\n    Quote: HBM demand is projected to grow roughly 70% year-over-year in 2026\",\n   \"- e215 [party_statement; tech-insider.org; original source Micron ; from gnews:8faf69f198e10f14aae67621 2026-07-12] Micron has suggested memory supply may not meaningfully normalize until 2027, with a gradual return to balance by 2028.\\n    Quote: Micron has since suggested supply may not meaningfully normalize until 2027, with a gradual return to balance by 2028\",\n   \"- e217 [party_statement; tech-insider.org; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:8faf69f198e10f14aae67621 2026-07-12] Nvidia said AWS plans to deploy 2 million additional Nvidia GPUs during 2027–2028.\\n    Quote: Nvidia said in August 2026 that AWS plans to deploy 2 million additional Nvidia GPUs in 2027 to 2028 .\",\n   \"- e218 [third_party_view; jpost.com; original source jpost.com 2026-07-12; from gnews:c14249088492921c802c839a 2026-07-12] NVIDIA's server GPU market share was about 97% at the end of calendar 2025, up from 95% at the end of 2024, according to the article.\\n    Quote: its market share climbing to about 97% at the end of 2025, compared to 95% the previous year\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e158; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e219 [fact; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] NVIDIA reported FY2027 Q1 total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: For the first quarter of fiscal 2027, revenue jumped 85% year-over-year (YOY) to $81.6 billion, easily beating analyst expectations.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e172, e229, e238; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e220 [fact; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] NVIDIA reported FY2027 Q1 Data Center revenue of $75.2 billion, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue climbed 92% YOY to $75.2 billion, highlighting that AI infrastructure remains the company's primary growth engine.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e193, e230; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e221 [party_statement; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] NVIDIA management forecast approximately $91 billion of revenue for FY2027 Q2, assuming no China Data Center sales.\\n    Quote: Management also issued strong guidance, forecasting approximately $91 billion in Q2 revenue despite assuming no China data-center sales because of export restrictions.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e168; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e222 [third_party_view; barchart.com; original source Wedbush Securities ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Wedbush Securities said NVIDIA's move into CPUs could significantly expand its total addressable market.\\n    Quote: Wedbush believes this move could significantly increase Nvidia's total addressable market.\",\n   \"- e223 [rumour; barchart.com; original source Unnamed reports ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Reports said NVIDIA had begun offering its Vera CPUs to cloud customers, including some in China where regulations allow.\\n    Quote: Reports also suggest Nvidia has begun offering the new processors to cloud customers, including some in China where regulations allow.\",\n   \"- e224 [third_party_view; barchart.com; original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Wall Street analysts expected NVIDIA FY2027 total revenue to exceed $300 billion; consensus EPS estimates were $8.80 per share.\\n    Quote: Wall Street expects Nvidia to generate well over $300 billion in fiscal 2027 revenue, while consensus earnings estimates have moved to $8.80 per share.\",\n   \"- e225 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source SK Hynix ; from gnews:03c38d2fe2e6e02ba5736307 2026-07-12] SK Hynix reported that quarterly revenue grew 198% to about $35 billion, a record, in the recent quarter.\\n    Quote: In the recent quarter, for example, the company reported revenue growth of 198% to about $35 billion dollars, a record level.\",\n   \"- e226 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source Counterpoint Research ; from gnews:03c38d2fe2e6e02ba5736307 2026-07-12] Counterpoint Research reported that SK Hynix held 58% of the global HBM market at the end of the first quarter.\\n    Quote: SK Hynix held 58% share globally of the HBM market as of the end of the first quarter, according to Counterpoint Research.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e181; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e227 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source SK Hynix and Nvidia ; from gnews:03c38d2fe2e6e02ba5736307 2026-07-12] SK Hynix and Nvidia signed a multi-year technology partnership under which SK Hynix will supply memory for areas including AI infrastructure, personal AI and robotics.\\n    Quote: The two companies even reinforced their relationship recently, signing a multi-year technology partnership. It involves SK Hynix supplying memory across a broad range of areas, from AI infrastructure to personal AI and robotics .\",\n   \"- e228 [party_statement; Jensen Huang, as quoted by fool.com (analyst); original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:03c38d2fe2e6e02ba5736307 2026-07-12] Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang said SK Hynix has been Nvidia's largest memory partner and will continue to be its largest memory partner.\\n    Quote: \\\"SK Hynix has been Nvidia's largest memory partner and will continue to be our largest memory partner,\\\" Nvidia chief Jensen Huang said at the time.\",\n   \"- e229 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:635f19578778394086009f6f 2026-07-12] NVIDIA reported record quarterly revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% quarter over quarter, in its fiscal quarter ended in late April.\\n    Quote: In its most recent fiscal quarter (ended in late April), revenue hit a record $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% from the prior quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e219; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e230 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:635f19578778394086009f6f 2026-07-12] NVIDIA reported data-center revenue of $75.2 billion, up 92% year over year, in its fiscal quarter ended in late April.\\n    Quote: Data center revenue of $75.2 billion climbed 92%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e220; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e231 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Broadcom ; from gnews:635f19578778394086009f6f 2026-07-12] Broadcom reported AI-chip revenue of $10.8 billion, up 143% year over year last quarter, and management forecast roughly $16 billion for this quarter.\\n    Quote: Its AI chip revenue jumped 143% year over year last quarter to $10.8 billion, and management sees roughly $16 billion this quarter.\",\n   \"- e237 [third_party_view; barchart.com; original source Bloomberg survey ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] A Bloomberg survey found Chinese technology companies expect domestic suppliers to receive roughly 46% of their AI-chip spending over the next year, up from about 30% currently.\\n    Quote: A new Bloomberg survey showed Chinese technology companies expect to allocate roughly 46% of their AI chip spending to domestic suppliers over the next year, up from about 30% currently.\",\n   \"- e238 [fact; barchart.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] Nvidia reported record FY2027 first-quarter revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: During the fiscal first quarter of 2027, Nvidia generated record revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year-over-year (YOY).\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e219; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e239 [party_statement; barchart.com; original source Nvidia management ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] Nvidia management guided fiscal second-quarter revenue to approximately $91 billion, assuming zero China data-center revenue because of export restrictions.\\n    Quote: Looking ahead, management guided Q2 revenue to approximately $91 billion, despite assuming zero China data-center revenue because of export restrictions.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e168; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e240 [third_party_view; barchart.com; original source Goldman Sachs ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] Goldman Sachs reiterated its Buy rating and $250 price target for Nvidia in May, citing evidence that enterprise AI spending remained healthy.\\n    Quote: In May, Goldman Sachs also reiterated its \\\"Buy\\\" rating on NVDA