erge; original source Xinzhou Wu, Nvidia head of automotive ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Nvidia automotive head Xinzhou Wu said automotive compute needs are growing roughly 10-fold every two years.\\n    Quote: Roughly we are talking about 10 times every two years. It’s insane.\",\n   \"- e244 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu, quoted by The Verge; original source Xinzhou Wu, Nvidia head of automotive ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said intense demand for chips would most likely require chip prices to rise.\\n    Quote: Actually, most likely even the chip price will need to go up, because of this intense demand for every chip everybody can grab onto.\",\n   \"- e245 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu, quoted by The Verge; original source Xinzhou Wu, Nvidia head of automotive ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said Nvidia was running five million tests per day in its autonomous-driving validation program.\\n    Quote: Right now we are looking at running five million tests in our program every day.\",\n   \"- e246 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu, quoted by The Verge; original source Xinzhou Wu, Nvidia head of automotive ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said Nvidia’s existing Drive partner program collects millions of hours of data and shares data with participating partners.\\n    Quote: For anybody who engages and becomes an Nvidia Drive partner, we share data through our existing program, through which we collect millions of hours of data.\",\n   \"- e247 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu, quoted by The Verge; original source Xinzhou Wu, Nvidia head of automotive ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said Tesla is ahead of competitors in the L2++ advanced driver-assistance market, citing its long-running development and testing across a massive fleet.\\n    Quote: For the basic L2++ technology, Elon is probably ahead of everybody. He had a division a long time ago and he has stuck to the vision for a long time to develop and test the technology among a massive fleet. Nobody would argue that Elon is ahead of everybody in the ADAS market and everybody is playing a catch-up game, essentially.\",\n   \"- e248 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu, quoted by The Verge; original source Xinzhou Wu, Nvidia head of automotive ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said Waymo is an established, proven Level 4 competitor already taking customers on rides using its approach.\\n    Quote: For Level 4, I think it’s more open. There are established players who are proven, like Waymo, who are already taking customers to really experience the L4 using the methodologies they use.\",\n   \"- e249 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu, quoted by The Verge; original source Xinzhou Wu, Nvidia head of automotive ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu predicted that Level 4 autonomy would become a mainstream car-buying experience in less than five years.\\n    Quote: I would say if I need to give a time, I wouldn’t say five years, but less than five years.\",\n   \"- e250 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu, quoted by The Verge; original source Xinzhou Wu, Nvidia head of automotive ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said Nvidia planned to roll out its ADAS technology in all Mercedes vehicles and vehicles from some other partners across the United States by the end of 2026.\\n    Quote: First of all, by the end of this year, we are rolling out our technology on the ADAS side in all Mercedes vehicles and some other partners as well, all over the United States.\",\n   \"- e251 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu, quoted by The Verge; original source Xinzhou Wu, Nvidia head of automotive ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said Nvidia and Uber were working to roll out an L4 service in the next few years.\\n    Quote: Meanwhile, we are also working closely with our partners, for example, Uber. We announced that at GTC, we are trying to roll out our L4 service in the next few years.\",\n   \"- e252 [party_statement; Xinzhou Wu, quoted by The Verge; original source Xinzhou Wu, Nvidia head of automotive ; from gnews:97740b9cee89425e62ea3526 2026-07-13] Wu said 80% of mass-production automakers were in Nvidia’s Hyperion ecosystem for Level 4 autonomy.\\n    Quote: Right now, I would say 80% of the mass-production OEMs are in Nvidia’s Hyperion ecosystem for L4.\",\n   \"- e253 [third_party_view; gurufocus.com; original source Citi ; from gnews:dedacecd6d2ed5192c307199 2026-07-13] Citi said Nvidia has strong access to high-bandwidth DRAM memory, a critical component for AI systems.\\n    Quote: The bank pointed to Nvidia's strong access to high-bandwidth DRAM memory, a critical component for AI systems.\",\n   \"- e256 [party_statement; gurufocus.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:dedacecd6d2ed5192c307199 2026-07-13] Nvidia expects sovereign AI projects and on-premise deployments to make up a larger share of future growth.\\n    Quote: It expects sovereign AI projects and on-premise deployments to make up a larger share of future growth as AI adoption expands.\",\n   \"- e258 [fact; fool.com author Stefon Walters; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:f4eb5206f2995f5dbb86c5e9 2026-07-13] Nvidia reported revenue of $81.6 billion for its quarter ended April 26, 2026, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: In its most recent quarter (ended April 26), it made $81.6 billion in revenue (up 85% year over year)\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e219, e281; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e259 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:3a9054a950c410e249837c91 2026-07-13] Nvidia reported record FY2027 Q1 revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% quarter over quarter.\\n    Quote: For its fiscal 2027 first quarter (ended April 26), Nvidia generated record revenue, up 85% year over year and 20% quarter over quarter to $81.6 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e229; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e260 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia ; from gnews:3a9054a950c410e249837c91 2026-07-13] Nvidia reported record data-center revenue of $75 billion in FY2027 Q1, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: The results were driven by record data center revenue of $75 billion, up 92%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e193; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e261 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Nvidia management ; from gnews:3a9054a950c410e249837c91 2026-07-13] Nvidia management forecast Q2 revenue of $91 billion, up 95% year over year.\\n    Quote: Management expects its growth spurt to continue, forecasting year-over-year revenue growth of 95% to $91 billion in Q2.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e174; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e262 [fact; 247WallSt author Alex Sirois; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:799ec454c15ddf61f08d042f 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.615 billion, up 85.23% year over year.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA’s Q1 FY2027 revenue reached $81.615 billion, up 85.23%\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e238; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e263 [fact; 247WallSt author Alex Sirois; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:799ec454c15ddf61f08d042f 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 Data Center revenue of $75.246 billion.\\n    Quote: Data Center at $75.246 billion\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e167; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e264 [fact; 247WallSt author Alex Sirois; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:799ec454c15ddf61f08d042f 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported that networking revenue grew 199% in Q1 FY2027.\\n    Qu