ginal source Alex Sirois 2026-07-13; from gnews:799ec454c15ddf61f08d042f 2026-07-13] Alex Sirois judged Broadcom better positioned than NVIDIA for the second half of 2026, citing faster AI-mix acceleration and the Apple relationship as support for Broadcom's custom-silicon business.\\n    Quote: For my own read, Broadcom looks like the better setup for the back half of 2026. The catalyst calendar is nearer, AI mix is accelerating faster off a smaller base, and the Apple relationship gives the ASIC thesis a marquee anchor.\",\n   \"- e271 [fact; 247wallst.com, Vandita Jadeja; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b68c019528300c6a1fcd3515 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported Data Center revenue of $75.246 billion for Q1 FY2027, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue hit $75.246 billion , up 92% YoY.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e220; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e272 [fact; 247wallst.com, Vandita Jadeja; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b68c019528300c6a1fcd3515 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported Data Center networking revenue of $14.8 billion for Q1 FY2027, up 199% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data Center networking alone did $14.8 billion, up 199%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e173; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e273 [fact; 247wallst.com, Vandita Jadeja; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b68c019528300c6a1fcd3515 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported total revenue of $81.615 billion for Q1 FY2027, up 85.2% year over year.\\n    Quote: Total revenue was $81.615 billion, growing 85.2%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e219; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e274 [fact; 247wallst.com, Vandita Jadeja; original source AMD ; from gnews:b68c019528300c6a1fcd3515 2026-07-13] AMD reported Data Center revenue of $5.775 billion for Q1 2026.\\n    Quote: Q1 2026 data center revenue of $5.775 billion.\",\n   \"- e275 [fact; 247wallst.com, Vandita Jadeja; original source Broadcom ; from gnews:b68c019528300c6a1fcd3515 2026-07-13] Broadcom reported AI semiconductor revenue of $10.8 billion for Q2 FY2026, up 143% year over year.\\n    Quote: Q2 FY26 AI semiconductor revenue was $10.8 billion, up 143% YoY\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e266; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e276 [party_statement; 247wallst.com, Vandita Jadeja; original source Hock Tan, Broadcom CEO ; from gnews:b68c019528300c6a1fcd3515 2026-07-13] Broadcom CEO Hock Tan targeted $100 billion in AI sales by 2027.\\n    Quote: CEO Hock Tan is targeting $100 billion in AI sales by 2027.\",\n   \"- e277 [fact; 247wallst.com, Vandita Jadeja; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b68c019528300c6a1fcd3515 2026-07-13] NVIDIA shipped no H20 compute products to China in Q1 FY2027.\\n    Quote: There were no H20 compute products shipped to China in Q1 FY27\",\n   \"- e278 [party_statement; 247wallst.com, Vandita Jadeja; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b68c019528300c6a1fcd3515 2026-07-13] NVIDIA's Q2 FY2027 guidance excluded Data Center compute revenue from China.\\n    Quote: the Q2 FY27 guidance excludes any Data Center compute revenue from China.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e175; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e279 [party_statement; 247wallst.com, Vandita Jadeja; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b68c019528300c6a1fcd3515 2026-07-13] NVIDIA guided to total revenue of $91 billion and a non-GAAP gross margin of 75% for Q2 FY2027.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA guided $91 billion for Q2 FY27 anyway, with a 75% non-GAAP gross margin.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e174; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e280 [party_statement; SCMP; original source Dongfang Suanxin 2026-07-13; from gnews:26712ffa8ed8118c6641a6f3 2026-07-13] Dongfang Suanxin announced a strategy based on software-defined computing and 3D-stacked near-memory architecture, which it said could reduce reliance on restricted advanced manufacturing processes and cutting-edge memory.\\n    Quote: The Shanghai-based firm announced on Monday that its strategy was built on software-defined computing and 3D-stacked near-memory architecture, which it said could reduce reliance on the advanced manufacturing processes and cutting-edge memory currently restricted by Washington.\",\n   \"- e281 [fact; 247wallst.com, Alex Sirois; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:221f52333c8f5e936e515c4d 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported revenue of $81.615 billion, up 85.23%, in the spring quarter; the item does not specify the fiscal quarter.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA ( NASDAQ: NVDA ) followed with $81.615 billion and 85.23% growth.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e258; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e282 [fact; 247wallst.com, Alex Sirois; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:221f52333c8f5e936e515c4d 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported Data Center revenue of $75.246 billion, up 92%, and Networking revenue growth of 199%, in the spring quarter; the item does not specify the fiscal quarter.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue hit $75.246 billion, up 92%, with Networking exploding 199%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e167; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e283 [fact; 247wallst.com, Alex Sirois; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:221f52333c8f5e936e515c4d 2026-07-13] NVIDIA shipped zero H20 chips to China this quarter, compared with $4.6 billion of H20 shipments a year earlier; the item does not specify the quarter.\\n    Quote: Yet zero H20 chips shipped to China this quarter, versus $4.6 billion a year ago.\",\n   \"- e284 [party_statement; 247wallst.com, Alex Sirois; original source Meta ; from gnews:221f52333c8f5e936e515c4d 2026-07-13] Meta raised its 2026 capital-expenditure guidance to $125 billion–$145 billion and launched Meta Compute, which rents excess internal AI capacity to external enterprises.\\n    Quote: Meta raised 2026 capex to $125 to $145 billion, then quietly launched Meta Compute, a service renting its excess internal AI capacity to external enterprises.\",\n   \"- e286 [party_statement; 247wallst.com, Alex Sirois; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:221f52333c8f5e936e515c4d 2026-07-13] NVIDIA guided to revenue of $91.0 billion, plus or minus 2%, excluding China, for Q2; the item does not specify the fiscal year.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA guided to $91.0 billion, plus or minus 2%, explicitly excluding China.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e239; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e287 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com; original source Dan Ives ; from gnews:221f52333c8f5e936e515c4d 2026-07-13] Dan Ives said NVIDIA demand is outpacing supply 12 to 1; the item gives no period for the estimate.\\n    Quote: Dan Ives Is Still Bullish on Nvidia: ‘We’re in the 3rd Inning of the AI Revolution,’ and Demand Is Outpacing Supply “12 to 1”\",\n   \"- e162 [party_statement; Trefis; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:6abaf2856736877236d30f6a 2026-07-10] NVIDIA guided revenue for the upcoming quarter to a midpoint of $91.00 billion.\\n    Quote: For the upcoming quarter, the company guided revenue to a midpoint of $91.00 billion, signaling continued strong demand.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e168, e329; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e168 [party_statement; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] NVIDIA guided to revenue of $91 billion for Q2 FY2027.\\n    Quote: Q2 FY27 guidance points to $91 billion in revenue.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e162, e221, e239, e315; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e172 [fact; 247WallSt. (David Moadel); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially, including Data Center revenue of $75.2 billion.\\n    Quote: The company reported record revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially, with Data Center revenue reaching $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e133, e219, e337; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e173 [fact; 247WallSt. (David Moadel); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA Data Center Networking revenue was $14.8 billion in Q1 FY2027, up 199% year over year.\\n    Quote: Within that segment, Data Center Networking alone hit $14.8 billion, up 199% from a year earlier, reflecting surging demand for the Spectrum-X Ethernet and NVLink interconnect systems that travel with every rack-scale Blackwell deployment.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e167, e264, e272, e312, e327; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e204 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source Mizuho Securities and Silicon Analysts ; from gnews:2beadbce40c7f927f33d9fc5 2026-07-12] Mizuho Securities estimated Nvidia's overall AI-chip market share at 70% to 95% depending on segment; Silicon Analysts projected it would settle near 75% as the total market grows beyond $200 billion.\\n    Quote: Nvidia 's overall AI chip market share, estimated by Mizuho Securities at between 70% and 95% depending on segment, is projected by Silicon Analysts to settle near 75% as the total market expands past $200 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e297; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e231 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Broadcom ; from gnews:635f19578778394086009f6f 2026-07-12] Broadcom reported AI-chip revenue of $10.8 billion, up 143% year over year last quarter, and management forecast roughly $16 billion for this quarter.\\n    Quote: Its AI chip revenue jumped 143% year over year last quarter to $10.8 billion, and management sees roughly $16 billion this quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e266, e267, e310; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e238 [fact; barchart.com; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] Nvidia reported record FY2027 first-quarter revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: During the fiscal first quarter of 2027, Nvidia generated record revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year-over-year (YOY).\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e219, e262, e326; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e239 [party_statement; barchart.com; original source Nvidia management ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] Nvidia management guided fiscal second-quarter revenue to approximately $91 billion, assuming zero China data-center revenue because of export restrictions.\\n    Quote: Looking ahead, management guided Q2 revenue to approximately $91 billion, despite assuming zero China data-center revenue because of export restrictions.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e168, e286, e336; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e262 [fact; 247WallSt author Alex Sirois; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:799ec454c15ddf61f08d042f 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.615 billion, up 85.23% year over year.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA’s Q1 FY2027 revenue reached $81.615 billion, up 85.23%\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e238, e331; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e271 [fact; 247wallst.com, Vandita Jadeja; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b68c019528300c6a1fcd3515 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported Data Center revenue of $75.246 billion for Q1 FY2027, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue hit $75.246 billion , up 92% YoY.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e220, e332; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e272 [fact; 247wallst.com, Vandita Jadeja; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b68c019528300c6a1fcd3515 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported Data Center networking revenue of $14.8 billion for Q1 FY2027, up 199% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data Center networking alone did $14.8 billion, up 199%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e173, e300; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e278 [party_statement; 247wallst.com, Vandita Jadeja; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b68c019528300c6a1fcd3515 2026-07-13] NVIDIA's Q2 FY2027 guidance excluded Data Center compute revenue from China.\\n    Quote: the Q2 FY27 guidance excludes any Data Center compute revenue from China.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e175, e314; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e289 [party_statement; Jeffery Kessler, quoted by CNBC; original source Jeffery Kessler, Under Secretary of Commerce for Industry and Security ; from gnews:9d898f2bf43ed52a98e1587a 2026-07-14] Under Secretary of Commerce for Industry and Security Jeffery Kessler said very few H200 and equivalent chips had shipped to China and Hong Kong under licenses.\\n    Quote: The bottom line is very few shipments against licenses for H200s and equivalents have taken place. It's a very small quantity of chips,\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e306, e351; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e291 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source TSMC ; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] TSMC raised its forecast for global semiconductor-market revenue by 2030 from $1 trillion, citing AI-fueled chip demand.\\n    Quote: The Taiwan-based foundry giant had previously anticipated $1 trillion in semiconductor revenue by the end of the decade. However, AI-fueled demand for chips led to a substantial upgrade to its guidance.\",\n   \"- e292 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source TSMC ; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] TSMC estimates AI and HPC chips will account for 55% of the projected global semiconductor-market revenue opportunity by 2030.\\n    Quote: TSMC points out that AI and high-performance computing (HPC) chips will account for 55% of this lucrative opportunity.\",\n   \"- e293 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Harsh Chauhan 2026-07-14; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] The author estimates NVIDIA's addressable AI data-center chip opportunity at $825 billion, based on TSMC's market forecast.\\n    Quote: That puts Nvidia's addressable opportunity in the AI data center chip market at an impressive $825 billion.\",\n   \"- e294 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported data-center revenue of $193.7 billion for FY2026, which ended in January 2026.\\n    Quote: For comparison, Nvidia's data center revenue in fiscal 2026 (which ended in January this year) was $193.7 billion.\",\n   \"- e295 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported FY2026 data-center compute-chip revenue of $162.3 billion; the remaining data-center revenue came from networking components.\\n    Quote: It is worth noting that $162.3 billion of its fiscal 2026 data center revenue came from sales of compute chips, while the rest was from networking components.\",\n   \"- e296 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Analysts ; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] Analysts believe NVIDIA's AI data-center chip market share may have peaked.\\n    Quote: However, analysts believe that Nvidia's AI data center chip market share may have peaked.\",\n   \"- e297 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Analysts ; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA's AI-chip market share is forecast to decline to 75% in 2026.\\n    Quote: That's why Nvidia's AI chip market share is anticipated to decline to 75% this year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e204; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e298 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Harsh Chauhan 2026-07-14; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] In the author's scenario, NVIDIA has 50% AI-chip market share in 2030 and generates more than $400 billion in data-center chip revenue that year, based on an $825 billion market estimate.\\n    Quote: Let's assume Nvidia continues to lose ground in AI chips for the next four years and ends up at just 50% market share in 2030; it can still generate more than $400 billion in data center chip revenue in 2030 (based on the $825 billion market size estimated above).\",\n   \"- e299 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported FY2026 networking revenue of $31.4 billion, up 142% year over year.\\n    Quote: The company reported a 142% year-over-year increase in networking revenue in fiscal 2026 to $31.4 billion.\",\n   \"- e300 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported networking revenue of $14.8 billion in the first quarter of FY2027, triple the year-earlier amount.\\n    Quote: It has started fiscal 2027 on a stronger note in this segment, with networking revenue tripling year-over-year to $14.8 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e272; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e301 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Mordor Intelligence ; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] Mordor Intelligence forecasts 36% annual growth in the InfiniBand market over the next five years.\\n    Quote: The InfiniBand market, for instance, is expected to clock 36% annual growth over the next five years, according to Mordor Intelligence.\",\n   \"- e302 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Mordor Intelligence ; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] The InfiniBand market is forecast to generate more than $164 billion in revenue in 2031.\\n    Quote: It could generate more than $164 billion in revenue in 2031.\",\n   \"- e303 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Dell'Oro Group ; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] Dell'Oro Group projects data-center switch-market revenue will exceed $100 billion by 2030.\\n    Quote: Meanwhile, the data center switch market is projected to exceed $100 billion in revenue by 2030, according to Dell'Oro Group.\",\n   \"- e304 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Harsh Chauhan 2026-07-14; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] The author estimates NVIDIA's combined data-center compute and networking addressable opportunity could exceed $1 trillion by 2030.\\n    Quote: In all, Nvidia's data center addressable opportunity, including both networking and compute, could surpass $1 trillion by the end of the decade.\",\n   \"- e305 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Analysts ; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] Analysts forecast NVIDIA FY2027 earnings per share of $8.97, up 88%.\\n    Quote: Analysts are projecting an 88% spike in Nvidia's earnings in fiscal 2027 (ending in January 2027) to $8.97 per share.\",\n   \"- e308 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:c73b90b63a733c6ab712fcdd 2026-07-14] NVIDIA management described the company's growth rates as accelerating while quarterly revenue neared $100 billion.\\n    Quote: management describing \\\"accelerating growth rates\\\" even as revenue nears $100 billion per quarter.\",\n   \"- e309 [fact; David Jagielski, CPA; original source Broadcom ; from gnews:cf6b0ccecbe4028542c4e178 2026-07-14] Broadcom’s growth rate was 48% in its most recent quarter, which ended May 3, 2026.\\n    Quote: Its growth rate was 48% in its most recent quarter (which ended May 3).\",\n   \"- e310 [fact; David Jagielski, CPA; original source Broadcom ; from gnews:cf6b0ccecbe4028542c4e178 2026-07-14] Broadcom said semiconductor revenue due to AI rose 143% in its most recent quarter, exceeding its forecast.\\n    Quote: the company says that semiconductor revenue due to AI rose by 143%, coming in even higher than its forecast.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e231; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e311 [fact; David Jagielski, CPA; original source AMD ; from gnews:cf6b0ccecbe4028542c4e178 2026-07-14] AMD reported revenue of $10.3 billion for the period ending March 28, 2026, up 38%.\\n    Quote: For the period ending March 28, the company's revenue rose by 38% to $10.3 billion.\",\n   \"- e312 [fact; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:1e1fa5a194198eaf05d90c9e 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.615 billion, up 85.23% year over year, and Data Center Networking revenue of $14.8 billion, up 199%.\\n    Quote: It delivered $81.615 billion in Q1 FY27 revenue, up 85.23% year over year, with Data Center Networking alone growing 199% YoY to $14.8 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e173, e333; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e313 [rumour; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source 247wallst.com (unnamed Reddit users, as reported by the author) ; from gnews:1e1fa5a194198eaf05d90c9e 2026-07-14] The author reports a rumor that DeepSeek is developing an in-house chip, a potential competitive threat to NVIDIA.\\n    Quote: The Reddit crowd has fixated on competitive threats, from DeepSeek’s rumored in-house chip to Meta’s $145B infrastructure budget aimed partly at custom silicon.\",\n   \"- e314 [party_statement; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:1e1fa5a194198eaf05d90c9e 2026-07-14] The author says NVIDIA's guidance excludes Data Center compute revenue from China.\\n    Quote: Guidance also excludes any Data Center compute revenue from China, a real overhang.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e278; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e315 [party_statement; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:1e1fa5a194198eaf05d90c9e 2026-07-14] The author cites quarterly earnings growth of 214.5% year over year and NVIDIA's Q2 FY2027 revenue guidance of $91 billion.\\n    Quote: With quarterly earnings growth of 214.5% YoY and Q2 FY27 revenue guided to $91 billion, the 12-month models remain anchored to yesterday’s earnings power.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e168; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e318 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Unspecified third-party estimates ; from gnews:37d2648cf990f4943cad6208 2026-07-14] The author cites third-party estimates that Nvidia controls 80% of the AI chip market; no estimate date or period is given.\\n    Quote: The good news is that Nvidia still controls an impressive 80% of the AI chip market, according to third-party estimates.\",\n   \"- e319 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Harsh Chauhan 2026-07-14; from gnews:37d2648cf990f4943cad6208 2026-07-14] The author says Nvidia’s AI-chip market position is gradually slipping as demand shifts from training to inference and competing chip technologies emerge; the author gives no market-share change or period for the decline.\\n    Quote: However, its control over this lucrative market is gradually slipping. The shift from AI training to inference and the emergence of competing chip technologies explain why Nvidia stock has risen just 8% this year despite sustaining impressive growth levels.\",\n   \"- e320 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Harsh Chauhan 2026-07-14; from gnews:37d2648cf990f4943cad6208 2026-07-14] The author says inference requires less computing power than training, a demand-mix change that could affect demand for Nvidia GPUs; no amount or period is specified.\\n    Quote: As a result, the inference phase doesn't require as much computing power as the training phase.\",\n   \"- e321 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Harsh Chauhan 2026-07-14; from gnews:37d2648cf990f4943cad6208 2026-07-14] The author says custom AI processors can perform designated tasks faster and with higher power efficiency than GPUs; no amount or period is specified.\\n    Quote: The specialized nature of these custom processors means they can perform their designated tasks faster than GPUs and with higher power efficiency.\",\n   \"- e322 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Harsh Chauhan 2026-07-14; from gnews:37d2648cf990f4943cad6208 2026-07-14] The author estimates Marvell controls 20% to 25% of the custom AI processor market; no estimate date or period is given.\\n    Quote: Marvell is one of the key players in custom AI processors, controlling 20% to 25% of this market.\",\n   \"- e323 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Marvell Technology ; from gnews:37d2648cf990f4943cad6208 2026-07-14] Marvell says it could pursue more than 50 custom AI chip opportunities across over 10 customers, with potential lifetime revenue of $75 billion; the timing is described only as the long run.\\n    Quote: In all, Marvell notes that it can tap into more than 50 custom AI chip opportunities across over 10 customers in the long run, leading to potential lifetime revenue of $75 billion.\",\n   \"- e326 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ac8a489e54fbb1b85a1c7a2c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85.2% year over year.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA’s Q1 FY27 revenue hit $81.6 billion, up 85.2% YoY\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e238; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e327 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ac8a489e54fbb1b85a1c7a2c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA Data Center Networking revenue grew 199% year over year, driven by InfiniBand, NVLink, and Spectrum-X pull-through.\\n    Quote: Data Center Networking alone growing 199% on InfiniBand, NVLink, and Spectrum-X pull-through.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e173; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e328 [party_statement; 247wallst.com; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:ac8a489e54fbb1b85a1c7a2c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said the buildout of AI factories was accelerating at extraordinary speed.\\n    Quote: “The buildout of AI factories, the largest infrastructure expansion in human history, is accelerating at extraordinary speed.”\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e334; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e329 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com; original source 247wallst.com 2026-07-14; from gnews:ac8a489e54fbb1b85a1c7a2c 2026-07-14] The author cited NVIDIA's forward P/E of 22x and PEG of 0.6, alongside company guidance for Q2 revenue of $91 billion.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA trades at a forward P/E of 22x with a PEG of 0.6, unusual for a company guiding to $91 billion in Q2 revenue.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e162; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e330 [fact; phoronix.com; original source System76 2026-07-14; from gnews:c6024d197f62679f8ff823a3 2026-07-14] System76 announced its new Adder Pro laptop with NVIDIA graphics; the laptop offers up to 96GB of RAM.\\n    Quote: System76 today announced their new Adder Pro laptop that they are promoting as the \\\"gamer's dream machine\\\" with its NVIDIA graphics, 2K OLED 500 nit display, up to 96GB RAM, and 3.37 lb weight.\",\n   \"- e331 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:184645c8d683d95b684bd6da 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.615 billion, up 85.23% year over year.\\n    Quote: Revenue hit $81.615 billion, up 85.23% YoY\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e262; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e332 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:184645c8d683d95b684bd6da 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 Data Center revenue of $75.246 billion, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data Center alone contributing $75.246 billion (+92% YoY).\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e271; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e333 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:184645c8d683d95b684bd6da 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 networking revenue of $14.8 billion, up 199% year over year.\\n    Quote: Networking was the sleeper hit at $14.8 billion (+199% YoY), driven by InfiniBand, Spectrum-X, and NVLink.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e312; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e334 [party_statement; Jensen Huang, quoted by 247wallst.com; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:184645c8d683d95b684bd6da 2026-07-14] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said AI-factory buildout was accelerating at extraordinary speed.\\n    Quote: “The buildout of AI factories , the largest infrastructure expansion in human history, is accelerating at extraordinary speed.”\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e328; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e336 [party_statement; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:184645c8d683d95b684bd6da 2026-07-14] NVIDIA guided to Q2 revenue of $91 billion; the author says the guidance assumes no China Data Center compute revenue.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA guided Q2 to $91 billion in revenue, which assumes zero China Data Center compute.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e239; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e337 [fact; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:386a294bd395bde25e3f4a11 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.61 billion, up 85.2% year over year, and Data Center revenue of $75.25 billion, up 92%.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA’s Q1 FY27 revenue hit $81.61B, up 85.2% YoY, with Data Center at $75.25B (+92%).\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e172; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e340 [fact; Rest of World; original source Saudi Arabia 2026-06-01; from gnews:01a49ffd41f6abe24538da65 2026-07-14] Saudi Arabia agreed on June 1 to use self-driving taxis running on Nvidia technology.\\n    Quote: Saudi Arabia agreed on June 1 to use self-driving taxis that run on Nvidia technology — from the computer inside each car to the software that steers it.\",\n   \"- e341 [fact; Rest of World; original source Humain ; from gnews:01a49ffd41f6abe24538da65 2026-07-14] Humain is building data centers in Riyadh and Dammam that are to be powered by several hundred thousand Nvidia chips.\\n    Quote: Humain is also building data centers in Riyadh and Dammam, powered by several hundred thousand Nvidia chips.\",\n   \"- e342 [fact; Rest of World; original source G42 ; from gnews:01a49ffd41f6abe24538da65 2026-07-14] G42 is building the Stargate data center in Abu Dhabi, whose first stage is planned to run on 400,000 Nvidia chips.\\n    Quote: The UAE is investing on the same scale through its state-backed AI firm G42, which is building a data center in Abu Dhabi called Stargate. Its first stage will run on 400,000 Nvidia chips .\",\n   \"- e343 [party_statement; Peng Xiao, quoted by Rest of World; original source Peng Xiao ; from gnews:01a49ffd41f6abe24538da65 2026-07-14] G42 CEO Peng Xiao said in a January interview that Nvidia chips would make up most of the machines inside Stargate.\\n    Quote: The machines inside Stargate would be “mostly” Nvidia, CEO Peng Xiao said in an interview in January.\",\n   \"- e344 [third_party_view; Kamil Dimmich, quoted by Rest of World; original source Kamil Dimmich ; from gnews:01a49ffd41f6abe24538da65 2026-07-14] Kamil Dimmich said Humain’s first Nvidia order was for 18,000 Blackwell chips.\\n    Quote: Humain’s first order from Nvidia was 18,000 of its newest Blackwell chips — the hardware that does that heavy lifting, which no rival can yet match, he said.\",\n   \"- e345 [third_party_view; Kamil Dimmich, quoted by Rest of World; original source Kamil Dimmich ; from gnews:01a49ffd41f6abe24538da65 2026-07-14] Kamil Dimmich said Qualcomm and Groq chips serve a narrower, cheaper inference role, while training powerful AI models still requires Nvidia chips.\\n    Quote: The deals give the Gulf chips that can run AI, but for a narrower set of tasks than those from Nvidia. The Qualcomm and Groq chips are built to run finished AI models cheaply, for everyday tasks like answering a user’s questions, while training a powerful model still calls for Nvidia’s chips, Kamil Dimmich, a partner at emerging-markets investment firm North of South Capital, told Rest of World .\",\n   \"- e346 [third_party_view; Kamil Dimmich, quoted by Rest of World; original source Kamil Dimmich ; from gnews:01a49ffd41f6abe24538da65 2026-07-14] Kamil Dimmich said Nvidia’s rivals rely on the same suppliers, with specialized high-speed memory and TSMC factory capacity among the hardest inputs to secure.\\n    Quote: Buying from a rival does not sidestep Nvidia in any case, because its competitors depend on the same suppliers further down the chain, Dimmich said. The two hardest things to secure are a specialized high-speed memory that keeps the chips fed with data, and space in the factories run by Taiwanese contract manufacturer TSMC, which makes chips for Nvidia and its rivals alike.\",\n   \"- e347 [third_party_view; Kamil Dimmich, quoted by Rest of World; original source Kamil Dimmich ; from gnews:01a49ffd41f6abe24538da65 2026-07-14] Kamil Dimmich said Nvidia chips remain essential for AI training, while cheaper ASICs for inference still depend on TSMC foundry capacity.\\n    Quote: “Nvidia chips are essential for training,” Dimmich said. “For this type of inference compute, increasingly there are ASIC [application-specific integrated circuit] designs that are cheaper than Nvidia but still need foundry capacity at TSMC.”\",\n   \"- e348 [fact; Tom's Hardware, relaying Reuters; original source U.S. government ; from gnews:3221eba2826b001b12b82770 2026-07-14] The U.S. government approved ZTE and Maginfra to buy Nvidia H200 chips; the item reports the approval on 2026-07-14.\\n    Quote: Today, Reuters reports that Chinese telecoms giant ZTE and server firm Maginfra have received U.S. approval to buy Nvidia's last-gen H200 \\\"Hopper\\\" chips.\",\n   \"- e350 [fact; Tom's Hardware, relaying Reuters; original source Chinese technology firms ; from gnews:3221eba2826b001b12b82770 2026-07-14] Reuters reported about six months before 2026-07-14 that Chinese technology firms had more than two million H200 chips on order, exceeding Nvidia's available inventory at the time.\\n    Quote: six months ago, Reuters said the nation's tech firms had more than two million H200 chips on order, far more than what Nvidia had on hand at the time.\",\n   \"- e351 [party_statement; Tom's Hardware, quoting CNBC's account of a congressional hearing; original source U.S. trade official 2026-07-14; from gnews:3221eba2826b001b12b82770 2026-07-14] A U.S. trade official said during a congressional hearing on 2026-07-14 that very few shipments had taken place under licenses for H200 chips and equivalents.\\n    Quote: CNBC cites a U.S. trade official who today stated that \\\"very few shipments against licenses for H200s and equivalents have taken place. It’s a very small quantity of chips\\\" during a congressional hearing.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e289; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e356 [fact; mlq.ai; original source FBI ; from gnews:ca7564a0dc63b215f5d49402 2026-07-14] The FBI issued an RFI seeking market input for AI supercomputer systems for its CJIS Division, including Nvidia Blackwell Ultra GPUs; the RFI is not a procurement commitment.\\n    Quote: The FBI has published a Request for Information on SAM.gov seeking market input on AI supercomputer hardware for its Criminal Justice Information Services (CJIS) Division in Clarksburg, West Virginia. The RFI outlines four distinct categories of accelerator systems spanning training, inference, and analytics workloads — including both Nvidia Blackwell Ultra GPUs and Google TPUs [1].\",\n   \"- e357 [third_party_view; mlq.ai; original source mlq.ai 2026-07-14; from gnews:ca7564a0dc63b215f5d49402 2026-07-14] Federal AI spending obligations reached $7.2 billion in 2026, compared with $675 million in 2024, according to the item.\\n    Quote: Federal AI spending obligations reached $7.2 billion in 2026, up from $675 million in 2024 — a 966% increase.\"\n  ]\n }\n]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; p=json.load(open(\\\"controls/control-packet-3.json\\\")); print(\\\"count\\\",len(p)); [(print(\\\"CONTROL\\\",x[\\\"control\\\"],\\\"\\\\nRULER\\\",x[\\\"ruler_question\\\"][\\\"question\\\"],x[\\\"ruler_question\\\"][\\\"due_day\\\"],\\\"\\\\nJUDGED\\\",x[\\\"judged_question\\\"],\\\"\\\\nITEMS\\\",json.dumps(x[\\\"reader_b_decisive_items\\\"],ensure_ascii=False))) for x in p]' \"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; p=json.load(open(\\\"controls/control-packet-3.json\\\")); print(\\\"count\\\",len(p)); [(print(\\\"CONTROL\\\",x[\\\"control\\\"],\\\"\\\\nRULER\\\",x[\\\"ruler_question\\\"][\\\"question\\\"],x[\\\"ruler_question\\\"][\\\"due_day\\\"],\\\"\\\\nJUDGED\\\",x[\\\"judged_question\\\"],\\\"\\\\nITEMS\\\",json.dumps(x[\\\"reader_b_decisive_items\\\"],ensure_ascii=False))) for x in p]' \"","aggregated_output":"count 1\nCONTROL 6 \nRULER What will Nvidia's total revenue be in FY2027? 2027-02-28 \nJUDGED {'view_id': 'v11', 'question': 'What will NVIDIA report as total revenue for FY2027?', 'looks_at': 'NVIDIA FY2027 total revenue', 'due_day': '2027-02-28', 'year': 'FY2027', 'kind': 'asset'} \nITEMS [{\"id\": \"i281\", \"day\": \"2026-07-09\", \"title\": \"DeepSeek Just Dealt Nvidia Stock a Potentially Major Blow\", \"passage\": \"forecasting revenue of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%, and a non-GAAP gross margin of about 75%\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"NVIDIA\", \"what\": \"Q2 FY2027 revenue and gross-margin guidance\", \"how_much\": \"$91 billion ±2%; non-GAAP gross margin about 75%\", \"period\": \"Q2 FY2027\", \"condition\": \"assumes no China Data Center compute revenue\", \"status\": \"forecast\"}}, {\"id\": \"i295\", \"day\": \"2026-07-10\", \"title\": \"Here are Friday's biggest analyst calls: Nvidia, SpaceX, Toll, Shopify, Twilio, Seagate, Chipotle & more\", \"passage\": \"the company describing \\\"accelerating growth rates\\\" even as revenues approach the $100 bn per quarter mark\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"NVIDIA management, relayed by Morgan Stanley\", \"what\": \"revenue growth rates accelerating\", \"how_much\": \"quarterly revenue approaching $100 bn\", \"status\": \"claim\"}}, {\"id\": \"i106\", \"day\": \"2026-07-05\", \"title\": \"Nvidia's next-gen AI rack system delayed to 2028 on manufacturing snags, SemiAnalysis says\", \"passage\": \"SemiAnalysis also projects Nvidia's data-center compute revenue will run 20% above Wall Street consensus in the second half of fiscal 2027\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"SemiAnalysis\", \"what\": \"NVIDIA data-center compute revenue versus Wall Street consensus\", \"how_much\": \"20% above consensus\", \"period\": \"second half of fiscal 2027\", \"status\": \"forecast\"}}, {\"id\": \"i219\", \"day\": \"2026-07-06\", \"title\": \"Nvidia Vera Rubin rack costs $7.8M — memory is why\", \"passage\": \"First shipments are scheduled for the third quarter of 2026, with volume ramping in the fourth.\", \"meaning\": {\"what\": \"Vera Rubin VR200 NVL72 first shipments and volume ramp\", \"period\": \"first shipments Q3 2026; volume ramp Q4 2026\", \"status\": \"plan\"}}, {\"id\": \"i037\", \"day\": \"2026-07-02\", \"title\": \"Microsoft vs. Nvidia: Which Is the Better AI Stock to Own for the Next 3 Years?\", \"passage\": \"from trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion to $392 billion this fiscal year, and $554 billion the following year\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"Wall Street analysts\", \"what\": \"NVIDIA total revenue estimates\", \"how_much\": \"$392 billion this fiscal year, $554 billion next year (from $253 billion trailing twelve months)\", \"period\": \"this fiscal year (FY2027) and the following year (FY2028)\", \"status\": \"forecast\"}}]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
